Short:        CopperNova CNP2 filesystem preview
Author:       Ilkka Lehtoranta
Uploader:     ilkleht@gmail.com (Ilkka Lehtoranta)
Type:         disk/misc
Version:      1.0-preview.3
Requires:     Kickstart and Workbench 3.1, 68000 or newer
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1

CopperNova is a new MIT-licensed Amiga filesystem written in C#.
This preview uses CNP2 root version 3 with wide extents and multi-group
allocation. It needs a TD64-capable device for the supplied disk image.
It supports creating, deleting and moving files and directories, file
reads and writes, enumeration, and explicit Flush.

Archive contents

CopperNovaPrototype  Native 68000 handler, embedded version CopperNova 1.0
BlankCNP2.rdb.gz     Freshly formatted 4 GiB + 64 MiB CNP2 partition
CopperNova.readme    This README
LICENSE.txt         MIT license
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt  CopperSharp license

Installation

1. Decompress BlankCNP2.rdb.gz on the host. Allow at least 4.1 GiB for
   the decompressed disk image. Keep a clean copy to start over if needed.
2. Boot Kickstart and Workbench 3.1 from your usual system disk. Attach
   the decompressed image as a second writable RDB hardfile or disk.
   The image already contains an installed copy of the handler and a
   formatted, nonbootable CNP0: partition with DOS type 0x434E5032 (CNP2).
3. Reboot if needed and check that CNP0: appears. Copy a test file to it,
   cleanly shut down, then boot again and verify the file.

Use a spare image or disk for the preview. Writing the full RDB image
to a physical disk overwrites its partition table and volume contents.
The preformatted image is the installation route exercised by the
Workbench test. A native DOS Format command and in-place conversion from
OFS, FFS, SFS or SFS2 are outside this preview.

Current limitations

- 512-byte sectors. The included full-disk partition is 4 GiB + 64 MiB.
  Larger geometries and physical controllers have yet to be qualified.
- Up to 1,022 live objects. Names are ASCII, with up to 168 bytes per
  component and a 255-byte DOS path. Each directory has 192 bytes for
  name records, which can limit it to a few entries with long names.
- Up to eight extents and 2 GiB minus one byte per file. A fragmented file
  can reach the extent limit before the disk fills.
- Links, sparse growth, grow-by-resize, extended attributes, notifications,
  record locking, automatic TRIM and removable-media change handling are
  outside this preview.
- Writes can be buffered. Use a clean shutdown or a successful explicit
  Flush before removing the volume. An interrupted in-place overwrite
  before Flush can leave a partially updated payload.
- Experimental images may need to be recreated for future releases.
  Keep independent copies of your files.

Qualification covers emulated Kickstart and Workbench 3.1, including RDB
discovery, TD64 transfers across 4 GiB, explicit Flush, cuts before both
publication barriers, and cold reads from durable sectors. The independent
checker verified allocation ownership and payload contents. Physical
hardware and storage qualification remain open.

Source code is at https://github.com/ilehtoranta/CopperFS
